 "e6_summary": "Without the cue, the duplicate rate on faults that a read-back resolves rises from 6\\% to 15\\% ($p=2\\times 10^{-8}$), on late commits from 55\\% to 68\\% ($p=3\\times 10^{-5}$), and on redelivery stays at 74\\% ($p=1.00$). On resolvable faults the change is concentrated in the weaker model, \\texttt{gpt-5.4-mini} (16\\% to 46\\%, $p=1\\times 10^{-6}$); the frontier models move from 4\\% to 7\\% ($p=0.01$). The explicit instruction therefore makes agents more careful, and the duplicate rates we report with it are conservative for instructions that leave exactly-once execution implicit.",
