 "guard_summary": "Transparent client-side retries cut exactly-once success from 77\\% to 51\\%. In the native contract even an outcome oracle that sees in-flight requests reaches only 88\\%, because redelivery on key-less writes is beyond any client-side policy; with keys on every write and a guard that attaches them, exactly-once success reaches 100\\%. The same holds in every harness: with keys everywhere, the duplicate rate of a shared model is at most 0\\% even without the guard, and exactly-once success is at least 100\\% with it."
